'''Dragon Talon''' is a [[fighting style]] that can be learned from [[Uzoth]] in the [[Third Sea]].

Dragon Talon serves as a direct upgrade from [[Dragon Breath]], with attacks that resemble [[Dragon]]'s abilities—hence the name. It focuses on close-range, high-damage, area-filled combat, utilizing burning effects and distorting the opponent’s view with violent screen shakes. 

However, in return, it is generally slower than most other [[Fighting Styles|fighting styles]]. Dragon Talon is mostly used for [[Raids]] and [[Dungeons]], or [[Sea Events]] due to its high damage and [[Area of Effect|AoE]] moves. Disabling screenshake also greatly aids the user, due to the high effect distortion on its moves. 

==Obtainment==
===Requirements===
* Have given the [[Uzoth]] NPC the [[Fire Essence]].
* At least 400 mastery on [[Dragon Breath]].
* {{Money|3,000,000}}
* {{Fragment|5,000}}

==Mastery== 
* At 400+ Mastery, Dragon Talon is one of the requirements to obtain [[Godhuman]] in [[Third Sea]].
* At 500+ Mastery, Dragon Talon is required to interact with the [[Dojo Trainer]].  To get [[Draco]] you need [[Dragonstorm]] and [[Dragonheart]] and getting them to 500 Mastery.
** After completing the [[Dojo Belt (Blue)|fifth quest]] from the [[Dojo Trainer]], the user can upgrade the style by collecting [[Blaze Ember]]s from the [[Dragon Hunter]], and then interacting with [[Uzoth]].

==Upgrading==
Dragon Talon's skillsets can be upgraded talking to [[Uzoth]] after obtaining the [[Dojo Belt (Blue)|Blue Belt]] from the [[Dojo Trainer]], prerequisite of having at least 500 Mastery on Dragon Talon. In order to obtain [[Blaze Ember]]s to upgrade Dragon Talon's skills, The player must talk to the [[Dragon Hunter]] and begin a quest, which, once completed, will reward them with [[Blaze Ember]]s.

* Upgrading '''[Z] Talon Lighter''' requires {{Blaze Ember|5}} [[Blaze Ember]]s, once upgraded, it allows the user to apply an execution/finisher move when they use it on an enemy with low health.
* Upgrading '''[X] Ember Annihilation''' requires {{Blaze Ember|7}} [[Blaze Ember]]s, which allows the user to mount with the flame dragon projectile if they hold the move.
* Upgrading '''[C] Infernal Vortex''' requires {{Blaze Ember|10}} [[Blaze Ember]]s, allows the user to stun nearby enemies during the startup of the move.

Upgrading all the moves require a total of {{Blaze Ember|22}} [[Blaze Ember]]s.

