==Overviews==
<tabber>
|-|Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Big hitboxes and AoE.
* High damage.
* High combo potential.
* All upgrades greatly aid the fighting style, only improving it.
* Great VFX.
* Deals high knockback to [[Lava Golem|Lava Golems]], making it easier to protect [[Ancient Relic]]. 

|'''[Z] Talon Lighter'''
* Can be used for mobility, holding it makes the player go further forward.
* Upgraded finisher ignores all defenses and all resurrection passives.
* Good hitbox.

|'''[X] Ember Annihilation'''
* Can curve at enemies (if the player moves the cursor) and can carry enemies to a certain distance.
* Drags enemies away while allowing the player to throw projectiles, or do combos on them.
* High range.
* Extremely high stun (3 seconds).
* Upgraded flight speed is quite fast, making it useful for traversal.

|'''[C] Infernal Vortex'''
* Very easy to land.
* Massive upward hitbox.
* Knocks enemies away, defending the user from combos.
* Upgrade adds a stun, making it even easier to land.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Hard to obtain.
* Close range.
* Weak in sea.
* High knockback, which can fling NPCs away (making it hard to farm) & players away, giving them a chance to escape.
* The fourth M1 pushes the user forwards, creating difficulties for grinding.
* Unlike [[Sharkman Karate]], upgrades cannot be turned off.

|'''[Z] Talon Lighter'''
* Single target. 
* Small hitbox making it hard to hit.
* Incompatible with [[Buddha]] due to its large size and hitbox, so the player has to aim down.
* Long finishers make kill stealing easy.
* No I-frames.
* High knockback.
* Low damage compared to other [[Fighting Style]] [Z] attacks.
* Low range. (Unless held.)

|'''[X] Ember Annihilation'''
* Quite slow, making it very weak at mid-range.
* Upgraded flight doesn't last very long.
* Very simple to [[Instinct]] trick.

|'''[C] Infernal Vortex'''
* Long startup time.
* The distortion effect can sometimes be annoying to users.
* Easy to avoid.
}}
