==Tips & Tricks== 
* If timed correctly, Dragon Talon can use two moves at once. By using {{Ability|Z}} and holding {{Ability|X}}, the user can ride the dragon while burning the opponent with {{Ability|Z}} (only works with the upgraded version). This is a glitch, so it might not work for some people and might get patched in a future update.
* There is a technique known as the Dragon Talon 360, where the player can use {{Ability|X}} and then change their character's facing direction to loop the projectile around and drag the opponent back towards them. To effectively do this, the player can aim {{Ability|X}} and, as it goes up, turn their camera to the ground they are on to execute the Dragon Talon 360.
** The trick can be followed up with the {{Ability|C}}  as a combo finisher.

* {{Ability|X}}'s stun is based on the Dragon's travel time. (more travel time = lower stun) 
** This makes it so if the player uses the skill on the ground (which makes it so it doesn't travel) the enemy cannot dash or use skills for roughly three seconds.
*** This makes it so that long windup but massive [[Area of Effect|AoE]] skills like [[Lightning]] {{Ability|Lightning|V}} or [[Flame]] {{Ability|Flame|V}} easier to hit
*'''[Z] Talon Lighter''' has a bug with large avatars, where it can launch players extremely high.

