==Trivia==
* Dragon Talon is famously used by [[Uzoth (Player)]], a content creator/admin of [[Blox Fruits Wiki|Blox Fruits]], and is considered to be his favourite [[Fighting Styles|fighting style]].
* Dragon Talon is the fighting style with the highest M1 damage in the game.
* Dragon Talon's M1 sound effects originated from [[Dragon Breath]]'s fire-based M1s, because its a predecessor to this fighting style.
* The finisher variant of {{Ability|Z}} is a ''guaranteed kill''—bypassing all forms of resurrection (like [[Ghost]]'s and [[Pain]]'s Resurrection passives, but also [[Friendly PvP]]'s revive), defense (like [[Shark]] V3 and [[Cyborg]] V3), healing (like [[Phoenix]]'s {{Ability|Phoenix|X}} and [[Angel]] V3), and [[instinct]]-tricking. 
** Additionally, the finisher variant of {{Ability|Z}} can ''chain'' through [[Cyborg]]'s awakened energy passives. 
* Dragon Talon's M1s release a mark that looks like a dragon's footprint.
* {{Ability|C}} resembles Transformed Eastern [[Dragon]]'s {{Ability|Dragon|X}}, as the user holds the enemy in place, jumps up, then slams down with devastating force.
* Contrary to popular belief, the head seen during {{Ability|Z}}, is a faint image of [[T-Rex]]'s head, not West [[Dragon]].
** This, combined with the fact that {{Ability|X}} uses East Dragon's model, and {{Ability|C}} resembling East Dragon's {{Ability|Dragon|X}}, Dragon Talon might have finished development prior to West Dragon.
* When the user uses {{Ability|X}} at a thin wall like the [[Ice Castle]]'s wall, they will have a slight chance of phasing through the wall.
* Dragon Talon is the first V2 [[Fighting Styles|Fighting Style]] to be able to be upgraded, followed by [[Sharkman Karate]].
* Dragon Talon has a bug where if the user uses {{Ability|C}} while they are swimming, they will immediately lose all their health (even while using [[Shark]] V2 or above). This also occasionally happens outside of water.
* When [[Instinct]] tricking {{Ability|Z}}, depending on when the user tricks it, they will either receive its traditional knockback, or simply fall out as they would when tricking most moves.

